{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCJMwpsodg4m29znA9aBmd","type":"tool_result","content":"=== run.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\nset -u\nD=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nT=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\nR=\"$D/runs/$T-$A-r$REP\"; rm -rf \"$R\"; mkdir -p \"$R\"\nW=$(mktemp -d /tmp/h-XXXXXX); cp -R \"$D/tasks/$T/.\" \"$W/\"\nP=\"$(cat \"$D/tasks/$T.prompt\")\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$P\" > \"$R/prompt.txt\"\nTO=1200\n\ncodex_run() {\n  ( cd \"$W\" && timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n      -o \"$R/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n}\n\n# Kimi's output goes to Moonshot: its shell runs under sandbox/agent.sb with an empty scratch HOME.\nkimi_run() {\n  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n      env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n      < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n  local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n}\n\nstart=$(date +%s)\ncase $A in\n  codex) codex_run;;\n  kimi)  kimi_run;;\n  *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\nesac\nrc=$?\nend=$(date +%s)\necho \"{\\\"task\\\":\\\"$T\\\",\\\"lane\\\":\\\"$A\\\",\\\"rep\\\":$REP,\\\"exit_code\\\":$rc,\\\"wall_s\\\":$((end-start))}\" > \"$R/meta.json\"\npython3 \"$D/check_answer.py\" \"$R\" > \"$R/answer.json\"\nrm -rf \"$W\"\necho \"$T-$A-r$REP rc=$rc answer=$(python3 -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('$R/answer.json'))['final']))\" 2>/dev/null) chars\"\n\n=== README.md\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n\n=== .gitignore\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\n\n=== check_answer.py\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\n\n=== sandbox/agent.sb\n;; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n\n=== tasks/fizz.prompt\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\n\n=== tasks/fizz/fizz.py\ndef fizz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\" \".join(fizz(i) for i in range(1, 16)))\n\nruns:\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   0 Nov  9 23:52 .keep\n\nsandbox:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 611 Nov  9 23:52 agent.sb\n\ntasks:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 fizz\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  82 Nov  9 23:52 fizz.prompt\n\ntasks/fizz:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 238 Nov  9 23:52 fizz.py\n\ntotal 16\ndrwx------  10 valentinakoniukhova wheel   320 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 698 root                wheel 22336 Nov  9 23:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 valentinakoniukhova wheel   384 Nov  9 23:52 .git\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel    19 Nov  9 23:52 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1174 Nov  9 23:52 README.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   938 Nov  9 23:52 check_answer.py\n-rwxr-xr-x   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1601 Nov  9 23:52 run.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 23:52 runs\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 23:52 sandbox\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 valentinakoniukhova wheel   128 Nov  9 23:52 tasks","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6460bfca-ad6a-4d37-adf4-60be93c03701","uuid":"29b6e62b-bdd4-4fbd-9693-c09af1963470","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:52:33.705Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== run.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# usage: run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]\n# lanes: codex   Codex CLI, unsandboxed\n#        kimi    Kimi Code under sandbox/agent.sb (no reading or writing the real home), scratch HOME\nset -u\nD=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nT=$1; A=$2; REP=${3:-1}\nR=\"$D/runs/$T-$A-r$REP\"; rm -rf \"$R\"; mkdir -p \"$R\"\nW=$(mktemp -d /tmp/h-XXXXXX); cp -R \"$D/tasks/$T/.\" \"$W/\"\nP=\"$(cat \"$D/tasks/$T.prompt\")\"; printf '%s\\n' \"$P\" > \"$R/prompt.txt\"\nTO=1200\n\ncodex_run() {\n  ( cd \"$W\" && timeout $TO codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C \"$W\" --json \\\n      -o \"$R/final.txt\" \"$P\" < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n}\n\n# Kimi's output goes to Moonshot: its shell runs under sandbox/agent.sb with an empty scratch HOME.\nkimi_run() {\n  local REAL=\"$HOME\" SH; SH=$(mktemp -d /tmp/khome-XXXXXX)\n  ( cd \"$W\" && export HOME=\"$SH\" && sandbox-exec -D HOME=\"$REAL\" -f \"$D/sandbox/agent.sb\" \\\n      env KIMI_CODE_HOME=\"$REAL/.kimi-code\" timeout $TO \"$REAL/.kimi-code/bin/kimi\" -p \"$P\" --output-format stream-json \\\n      < /dev/null > \"$R/agent.log\" 2> \"$R/agent.err\" )\n  local rc=$?; rm -rf \"$SH\"; return $rc\n}\n\nstart=$(date +%s)\ncase $A in\n  codex) codex_run;;\n  kimi)  kimi_run;;\n  *) echo \"unknown lane $A\"; exit 2;;\nesac\nrc=$?\nend=$(date +%s)\necho \"{\\\"task\\\":\\\"$T\\\",\\\"lane\\\":\\\"$A\\\",\\\"rep\\\":$REP,\\\"exit_code\\\":$rc,\\\"wall_s\\\":$((end-start))}\" > \"$R/meta.json\"\npython3 \"$D/check_answer.py\" \"$R\" > \"$R/answer.json\"\nrm -rf \"$W\"\necho \"$T-$A-r$REP rc=$rc answer=$(python3 -c \"import json;print(len(json.load(open('$R/answer.json'))['final']))\" 2>/dev/null) chars\"\n\n=== README.md\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n\n=== .gitignore\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\n\n=== check_answer.py\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\n\n=== sandbox/agent.sb\n;; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n\n=== tasks/fizz.prompt\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\n\n=== tasks/fizz/fizz.py\ndef fizz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\" \".join(fizz(i) for i in range(1, 16)))\n\nruns:\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   0 Nov  9 23:52 .keep\n\nsandbox:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 611 Nov  9 23:52 agent.sb\n\ntasks:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 fizz\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  82 Nov  9 23:52 fizz.prompt\n\ntasks/fizz:\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 valentinakoniukhova wheel 128 Nov  9 23:52 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 valentinakoniukhova wheel 238 Nov  9 23:52 fizz.py\n\ntotal 16\ndrwx------  10 valentinakoniukhova wheel   320 Nov  9 23:52 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 698 root                wheel 22336 Nov  9 23:52 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 valentinakoniukhova wheel   384 Nov  9 23:52 .git\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel    19 Nov  9 23:52 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1174 Nov  9 23:52 README.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   938 Nov  9 23:52 check_answer.py\n-rwxr-xr-x   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1601 Nov  9 23:52 run.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 23:52 runs\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 23:52 sandbox\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 valentinakoniukhova wheel   128 Nov  9 23:52 tasks","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SCJMwpsodg4m29znA9aBmd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
