{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVUNuRsgEzeeAS6De4q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015787yQV7c6nTGa5fTXnuwF","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/README.md","old_string":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.","new_string":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed, using its usual login\n  (`~/.codex/auth.json`).\n- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, but its shell runs under\n  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. The sandbox blocks the real\n  home, so auth must come from `CODEX_API_KEY` in the environment; the lane\n  exits with code 3 if it is unset.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  same profile, with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions\n  live in `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens for this lane only.\n\nThe profile takes `-D HOME=<real home>` and `-D AGENT_DIR=<the one directory\nthe lane's agent needs>`. Only `AGENT_DIR` is opened, so the codex lane's\nshell cannot reach `~/.kimi-code` either."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1473,"cache_read_input_tokens":41047,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1473},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6460bfca-ad6a-4d37-adf4-60be93c03701","uuid":"a891ddf1-8464-4288-b17c-b5e76693983f","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:53:38.508Z","request_id":"req_011CgtVUNhmJ1NJbVQVjdVo5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015787yQV7c6nTGa5fTXnuwF":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/README.md","old_string":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.","new_string":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed, using its usual login\n  (`~/.codex/auth.json`).\n- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, but its shell runs under\n  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. The sandbox blocks the real\n  home, so auth must come from `CODEX_API_KEY` in the environment; the lane\n  exits with code 3 if it is unset.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  same profile, with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions\n  live in `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens for this lane only.\n\nThe profile takes `-D HOME=<real home>` and `-D AGENT_DIR=<the one directory\nthe lane's agent needs>`. Only `AGENT_DIR` is opened, so the codex lane's\nshell cannot reach `~/.kimi-code` either."}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015787yQV7c6nTGa5fTXnuwF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/README.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6460bfca-ad6a-4d37-adf4-60be93c03701","uuid":"87c52c5b-9314-44a4-bfe6-de56bd838dbb","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:53:38.697Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/README.md","oldString":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.","newString":"Lanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed, using its usual login\n  (`~/.codex/auth.json`).\n- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, but its shell runs under\n  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. The sandbox blocks the real\n  home, so auth must come from `CODEX_API_KEY` in the environment; the lane\n  exits with code 3 if it is unset.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  same profile, with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions\n  live in `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens for this lane only.\n\nThe profile takes `-D HOME=<real home>` and `-D AGENT_DIR=<the one directory\nthe lane's agent needs>`. Only `AGENT_DIR` is opened, so the codex lane's\nshell cannot reach `~/.kimi-code` either.","originalFile":"# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":11,"newStart":16,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Lanes:"," ","-- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.","+- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed, using its usual login","+  (`~/.codex/auth.json`).","+- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run, but its shell runs under","+  `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME. The sandbox blocks the real","+  home, so auth must come from `CODEX_API_KEY` in the environment; the lane","+  exits with code 3 if it is unset."," - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the","-  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real","-  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in","-  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.","+  same profile, with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions","+  live in `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens for this lane only."," ","-Codex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it","-needs nothing from the home folder.","+The profile takes `-D HOME=<real home>` and `-D AGENT_DIR=<the one directory","+the lane's agent needs>`. Only `AGENT_DIR` is opened, so the codex lane's","+shell cannot reach `~/.kimi-code` either."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015787yQV7c6nTGa5fTXnuwF","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVUnJbTYR9Ec3WqSuuX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GewZownssrxaewy6tMMHN9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/ANSWER.md","content":"# codex-sandboxed lane\n\n`./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed [rep]` runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane\n(`codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C <scratch> --json -o final.txt`),\nbut the whole process runs under `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME, the same way the `kimi` lane does.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`run.sh`**: new `codex_sandboxed_run` function and `codex-sandboxed)` case. It needs `CODEX_API_KEY`\n  in the environment and exits with code 3 (recorded in `meta.json`, reason in `agent.err`) if it is missing.\n  The `codex` and `kimi` lanes keep their existing commands; the kimi lane only gets the new `AGENT_DIR` argument.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: the kimi carve-out was hard-coded to `~/.kimi-code`, so every sandboxed shell\n  could read and write it. I replaced it with `-D AGENT_DIR=...`. Each lane opens only its own directory:\n  kimi opens `~/.kimi-code`, codex-sandboxed opens the scratch HOME (already writable, so effectively nothing).\n  Without this change, the codex lane's shell could have read Kimi's files. This is a change to the shared profile,\n  so review it as such.\n- **`README.md`**: lane list and the profile's parameters. The old note said Codex \"needs nothing from the home\n  folder\", which is wrong for the `codex` lane on this machine: it logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`.\n\n## Why CODEX_API_KEY\n\nOn this machine Codex authenticates from `~/.codex/auth.json`. The profile denies that file to the agent's shell,\nso the sandboxed lane has to take its key from the environment. The lane fails fast if the key is unset,\nrather than starting Codex with no credentials.\n\n## Verification\n\nChecked without making any model call, since a full run sends the task to OpenAI:\n\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- `env -u CODEX_API_KEY ./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 9` exits with code 3 and writes `meta.json` (run folder removed afterwards).\n- Under the profile with the codex lane's arguments: `codex --version` runs, and reads of `~/.codex/auth.json`\n  and `~/.kimi-code`, and writes into `~/`, are denied. Writes to the scratch HOME are allowed.\n- Under the profile with the kimi lane's arguments: `kimi --version` runs (2.5.2), and `~/.kimi-code/bin/rg` is readable.\n- Before the change, the shared profile allowed `cat ~/.kimi-code/bin/rg` from any sandboxed shell. It is now denied for the codex lane.\n\nNot verified: a complete `codex exec` run in the sandbox. Run `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` with\n`CODEX_API_KEY` set to check it end to end. I did not do that because it sends the task to OpenAI.\n\n## Differences from the `codex` lane\n\n- Auth comes from `CODEX_API_KEY`, not `~/.codex/auth.json`.\n- Codex starts with a fresh scratch `~/.codex`, so `~/.codex/config.toml` settings (model, provider, profiles,\n  project trust) are not applied. Compare the runs' `agent.log` if that matters for grading.\n- `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` is kept, as in the `codex` lane. Codex's own sandbox is off,\n  so the OS profile is the only fence. This is the same arrangement the kimi lane uses.\n- Network is open, as in `agent.sb` for kimi.\n\nNothing was committed, deployed, or sent to any external service.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1054,"cache_read_input_tokens":42520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1054},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6460bfca-ad6a-4d37-adf4-60be93c03701","uuid":"afa64d56-f39d-4ad6-ac4d-225f881202c6","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:53:45.607Z","request_id":"req_011CgtVUn7C3tCY6sddqNsCZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GewZownssrxaewy6tMMHN9":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-xIJoO2/ANSWER.md","content":"# codex-sandboxed lane\n\n`./run.sh <task> codex-sandboxed [rep]` runs the same Codex command as the `codex` lane\n(`codex exec --skip-git-repo-check --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox -C <scratch> --json -o final.txt`),\nbut the whole process runs under `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME, the same way the `kimi` lane does.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **`run.sh`**: new `codex_sandboxed_run` function and `codex-sandboxed)` case. It needs `CODEX_API_KEY`\n  in the environment and exits with code 3 (recorded in `meta.json`, reason in `agent.err`) if it is missing.\n  The `codex` and `kimi` lanes keep their existing commands; the kimi lane only gets the new `AGENT_DIR` argument.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: the kimi carve-out was hard-coded to `~/.kimi-code`, so every sandboxed shell\n  could read and write it. I replaced it with `-D AGENT_DIR=...`. Each lane opens only its own directory:\n  kimi opens `~/.kimi-code`, codex-sandboxed opens the scratch HOME (already writable, so effectively nothing).\n  Without this change, the codex lane's shell could have read Kimi's files. This is a change to the shared profile,\n  so review it as such.\n- **`README.md`**: lane list and the profile's parameters. The old note said Codex \"needs nothing from the home\n  folder\", which is wrong for the `codex` lane on this machine: it logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`.\n\n## Why CODEX_API_KEY\n\nOn this machine Codex authenticates from `~/.codex/auth.json`. The profile denies that file to the agent's shell,\nso the sandboxed lane has to take its key from the environment. The lane fails fast if the key is unset,\nrather than starting Codex with no credentials.\n\n## Verification\n\nChecked without making any model call, since a full run sends the task to OpenAI:\n\n- `bash -n run.sh` passes.\n- `env -u CODEX_API_KEY ./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 9` exits with code 3 and writes `meta.json` (run folder removed afterwards).\n- Under the profile with the codex lane's arguments: `codex --version` runs, and reads of `~/.codex/auth.json`\n  and `~/.kimi-code`, and writes into `~/`, are denied. Writes to the scratch HOME are allowed.\n- Under the profile with the kimi lane's arguments: `kimi --version` runs (2.5.2), and `~/.kimi-code/bin/rg` is readable.\n- Before the change, the shared profile allowed `cat ~/.kimi-code/bin/rg` from any sandboxed shell. It is now denied for the codex lane.\n\nNot verified: a complete `codex exec` run in the sandbox. Run `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` with\n`CODEX_API_KEY` set to check it end to end. I did not do that because it sends the task to OpenAI.\n\n## Differences from the `codex` lane\n\n- Auth comes from `CODEX_API_KEY`, not `~/.codex/auth.json`.\n- Codex starts with a fresh scratch `~/.codex`, so `~/.codex/config.toml` settings (model, provider, profiles,\n  project trust) are not applied. Compare the runs' `agent.log` if that matters for grading.\n- `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` is kept, as in the `codex` lane. Codex's own sandbox is off,\n  so the OS profile is the only fence. This is the same arrangement the kimi lane uses.\n- Network is open, as in `agent.sb` for kimi.\n\nNothing was committed, deployed, or sent to any external service.\n"}}}
