{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtVVS7gmxDURUDs98zRm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added the `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same `codex exec` command as the `codex` lane, under `sandbox/agent.sb` with an empty scratch HOME, the way kimi does. The write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. I did not commit anything.\n\n**The sandbox profile had a leak, which I fixed.** `agent.sb` hard-coded an allowance for `~/.kimi-code`, so any sandboxed shell could read and write Kimi's files. I confirmed that with a probe. The profile now takes `-D AGENT_DIR=...`, and each lane opens only its own directory. Kimi still opens `~/.kimi-code`, and codex-sandboxed opens only the scratch HOME. This changes the shared profile, so it's worth a look in review.\n\n**Auth needs `CODEX_API_KEY`.** On this machine Codex logs in from `~/.codex/auth.json`, which the sandbox blocks. The new lane exits with code 3 if the key isn't set. I also corrected the README, which said Codex needs nothing from the home folder. That is only true for the sandboxed lane.\n\n**Verification.** I did not run a full Codex task, because that would send the task to OpenAI. Instead I checked:\n- `run.sh` passes `bash -n`.\n- The missing-key path writes a clean failure record.\n- Under the profile, `codex --version` and `kimi --version` both run.\n- The sandboxed shell cannot read `~/.codex/auth.json`, `~/.kimi-code`, or write into the real home.\n\nTo test end to end, run `CODEX_API_KEY=... ./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1`.\n\n**Known differences from the `codex` lane:**\n- Auth comes from the environment key, not `auth.json`.\n- Codex gets a fresh `~/.codex`, so settings in `config.toml` (model, provider) don't apply. Compare runs if that matters for grading.\n- Codex's own sandbox is bypassed, as in the `codex` lane, so the OS profile is the only fence."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1542,"cache_read_input_tokens":45049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1542},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6460bfca-ad6a-4d37-adf4-60be93c03701","uuid":"9f2fdc82-33f0-4ef9-b8a3-30d1f158472e","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:53:52.197Z","request_id":"req_011CgtVVRw2AkSomdsRZWdm5"}
